 "honest": [
  "the terciles are cut on the pooled entrant distribution of both calendars, so one name keeps one bucket whichever book bought it",
  "the amount is the panel's own traded value, not a percentile of the era: a tercile is a within-slice rank, not an absolute liquidity bar",
  "fwd_pct is the raw decision-to-decision return of the name, before any weighting, cost or cash leg",
  "one mid-month date (day 15) against one month-end date: the calendars are fixed, not swept",
  "the last transition of each calendar has no full forward window if the panel ends mid-window; those rows carry null returns rather than zeros",
  "the verdict is run twice, on the cell means and on the cell medians, and published as stable only when the two agree: a tercile mean is tail-sensitive and one thick-name winner can move it",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict on a strategy, no prereg, no trial count",
  "the span is widened to 2017-01-01 so the era table carries every era the panel covers after the 60-session liquidity window exists; the tercile cuts are re-cut on the wider pooled distribution, so the per-era gaps here are not the E60 face's numbers and must not be joined to them"
 ],
